<title>CHILE: Chile Nov copper exports slump on lower prices.</title>
<headline>Chile Nov copper exports slump on lower prices.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper exports tumbled in November to $501.6 million from $663 million in the same month last year as the result of the slide in world copper prices, said the Central Bank.</p>
<p>METAL			   Nov 1996	    Nov 1995</p>
<p>Copper			  501.6		 663.1</p>
<p>Iron			     20.4		  14.0</p>
<p>Salitre and iodine	   13.5		   7.6</p>
<p>Silver			   11.6		   8.5</p>
<p>Molybdenum		     17.3		  33.5</p>
<p>Lithium carbonate	     3.5		   3.2</p>
<p>Metallic gold and dore     32.8		  31.4</p>
<p>Gold mineral		    0.0		   3.9</p>
<p>Others			    6.2		   8.2</p>
<p>TOTAL			   606.9		 710.8</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
</text>
